From ffa6e58eb0e7f5ca7ebfb30562a44c4103baf55d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:57:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/16] x86/mic: KNC memory management

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6:
 - 64k pages: native_set_pte() replicates a 64k mapping over its 16
   4k slots, the KNC _PAGE_* bits (pgtable_types.h) and the hugetlb
   arch_make_huge_pte() for 2M/64k pages.
 - Instruction-cache coherence: KNC does not snoop the icache on
   stores, so mapping a page executable flushes it
   (mic_flush_icache_nonx from mk_pte(), the cacheflush syscall in
   mic_cacheflush.c, decompressor stub).

Adaptations for 6.18:
 - mk_pte()/folio_mk_pte() are generic in mm.h since 6.x; the
   EARLYMIC variants keep the icache flush there.
 - __native_tlb_flush_global() (5.17/6.0) toggles CR4.PGE, which is
   reserved on KNC: it is a CR3 reload on EARLYMIC (flushes everything
   without global pages). 5.15 never hit this because every flush
   path was guarded by X86_FEATURE_PGE.
 - arch_make_huge_pte(entry, shift, flags) (5.14); native_set_pte 64k
   expansion folded into upstream's WRITE_ONCE variant (4.19).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
